WEBVTT

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.510
Class is finally over!

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:09.660
It's a three-day weekend!

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.040
Where should we go?

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.580
Oh, Inaba...

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.090
Any plans for the three-day weekend?

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:19.370
Work.

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:21.180
All three days?

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.310
Even though it's a three-day weekend?

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:25.330
Let's hang out!

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.450
I'm broke, guys.

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:30.250
<i>I need rent money, or else!</i>

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:37.090
<b>Book of Blessings</b>

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.240
I'm sorry, landlord!

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:39.160
I'll do my best.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:15.320
<b>Eighteenth Haunting 
Words From Deep Within Your Body</b>

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:16.400
<b>Kenzaki Transport</b>

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:18.320
Morning!

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:21.180
Oh, Inaba... Morning.

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:22.280
Yama-san!

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:23.890
Good morning.

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:26.400
Yushi, we've been waiting for you.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.820
Working on your three-day 
weekend is a big help.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:30.000
It helps me, too.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.810
I'm going to make a lot of money.

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.910
Yeah, do that.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:37.950
Hey, he's here.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:40.720
Let's work hard on this three-day weekend!

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:42.340
We're counting on you!

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:46.430
Stop it...

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:47.390
Right, right.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:50.350
How long will you sit around the office?

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:52.760
Shimazu-neesan, good morning.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:56.030
Good morning. It's almost time to start work.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.210
Get changed, Inaba-kun.

00:02:58.210 --> 00:02:59.870
And clock in.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:00.950
R-Right!

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.180
Boss, please get that paperwork done.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:05.270
Yes, yes... Right away!

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:09.100
Oh, yeah. Yushi, got a second?

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:09.990
Sure.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:13.040
<b>Kenzaki Transport</b>

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:13.040
Hey, guys, come here.

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:16.210
These guys are new part-timers.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:19.630
I'm Yushi Inaba! It's nice to meet you!

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:22.300
Hi.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:24.610
Um...

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:28.690
The blond is Sasaki, and the one 
with glasses is Kawashima.

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:30.390
They're both in college.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:32.670
Sasaki-san and Kawashima-san.

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:34.060
Roger.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.980
So, Yushi, I want you to show them the ropes.

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:40.740
But I'm younger!

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:43.760
You've been here over a year, right?

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:45.770
So here, you're the senpai.

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:47.990
That's true, but...

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:50.410
It'll be fine. I'm counting on you.

00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:55.000
Okay, let's get you guys started.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.000
<i>I'm really nervous!</i>

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:04.090
<i>Yama-san's crazy, sometimes...</i>

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:10.430
<i>I can't tell if they're listening 
to me or not.</i>

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:13.350
<i>Will this be all right?</i>

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:20.190
<i>They're doing their job correctly.</i>

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:23.110
<i>They were listening to me.</i>

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:28.620
Oh, Kawashima-san...

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:32.120
Use the dolly, or you'll hurt your back.

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:36.250
You're allowed to use the dolly?

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:38.290
No, no.

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:41.050
It belongs to everyone, so you 
can use it when you want.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:41.860
I see.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:43.010
Okay.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:44.690
Don't worry about it.

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:46.640
Then, I'll take these.

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.230
Yeah. Thanks.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.560
<i>There's something weird about that guy...</i>

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:57.980
It is great to see you so 
hard at work, master.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:04:59.310
I didn't call you.

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:04.560
A first-rate servant is there for his master, 
even when he isn't called!

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.530
And just who is a first-rate servant?

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:10.440
It appears you are doing physical labor.

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:15.910
This is when you should turn to the 
<i>Petit Hierozoicon</i>! For example...

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:22.680
Goyelems, the stone doll, can carry anything!

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:25.800
I bet that's what would happen.

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:29.140
Th-Then, how about Jin, 
the omnipotent spirit?

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:31.240
It would be over in an instant!

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:35.480
He'll only work up to 500 yen, though.

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:40.810
He went home!

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:45.740
Then, use the power of Brondis, the judge,
 to blow the packages away!

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.490
What do you think those packages are?!

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:53.290
Master, please don't leave me in here.

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:55.150
Sorry, Fool.

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:58.460
We aren't allowed to use phones 
or magic books at work.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:00.330
Oh? Is that a real rule?

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:01.790
Of course not.

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:03.970
It's so dark!

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:06.650
Master, rely on us more!

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:09.000
Be quiet until my shift is over.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.140
Do not leave us, master!

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:15.560
<b>Kenzaki Transport</b>

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:13.970
Okay, lunchtime!

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:15.560
Right!

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:24.930
<i>At times like these, I thought 
opening up to them might be better.</i>

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:27.410
<i>But this sense of distance...</i>

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:32.410
<i>Maybe it's a bit similar.</i>

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:36.750
Hey, the afternoon batch is here!

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:38.130
Right!

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:42.580
Are you two done eating?

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:43.460
Yeah.

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:44.430
Yeah.

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:48.010
Then, Sasaki-san, you bring the box.

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:50.680
I'll pass the packages to you, Kawashima-san.

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:53.010
What's wrong?

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:56.720
<b>Tea</b>

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:57.510
What do we do with the trash?

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:00.790
The trash can's over there! Hurry!

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:02.080
Okay.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:06.780
I knew this wasn't working!

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:21.210
It's over...

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:24.380
Good work.

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:25.280
Here.

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:27.330
It's cold.

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:28.380
Here.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:29.360
Here.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:32.320
My treat.

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:34.330
See you tomorrow.

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:37.220
Th-Thank you very much!

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:40.170
U-Um...

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:42.900
Thank you... very much.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:44.350
They'll get warm.

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:45.810
Drink up, quick!

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:47.230
Right!

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:53.070
So good!

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:57.930
This really is good.

00:07:57.930 --> 00:07:58.990
Yeah.

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:08.250
Cheers!

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:11.170
That's a nice story!

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:12.340
Is it?

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:14.140
It is.

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:16.870
Young men working as hard as they can,

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:20.770
then grinning, after receiving 
some delicious coffee...

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:23.200
Youth!

00:08:23.570 --> 00:08:25.350
Youth, huh?

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:29.960
Those two learned how to 
communicate with their bodies.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:32.530
How to say thank you!

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:33.950
That's right.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:37.320
You need to learn to speak with your body.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:39.450
You're right!

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:42.750
Learn to speak... with your body?

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:46.630
Thanks, Ruriko-san.

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:48.300
Let's drink.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:54.060
These days,

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:57.970
from birth, you're surrounded 
by information, right?

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:03.050
But that means you don't develop the important
 skill of how to learn information.

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:05.310
How to learn information?

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:11.570
<b>Treasure Map</b>

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:11.650
Information isn't supposed to be 
something you're given.

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:16.820
It's the reward you get for showing interest 
in something and taking action.

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:21.330
Of course, action doesn't 
always equal reward.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:25.370
Sometimes, a thing can be less than imagined.

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:28.720
But because of that effort you put in,

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:31.090
it becomes something that teaches you.

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:34.970
Sasaki-kun and Kawashima-kun were

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:38.240
happy to receive coffee as a 
reward for their efforts.

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:41.100
The "thank you" issuing from their lips

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:44.010
was something that came from their bodies.

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:48.190
I doubt they'll ever forget 
the taste of today's coffee.

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:57.880
Words that come from the body, huh?

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:06.590
Crap.

00:10:06.590 --> 00:10:08.200
I totally forgot.

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:14.000
Master, do you hate me?

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:17.970
No, I don't! Today, I was, um...

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:20.420
I was so busy, I forgot...

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:25.220
A-All right. Is that what happened?

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:25.930
I'm sorry!

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:27.370
Master!

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:30.300
Don't you think you should treat us better?!

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:31.860
I'm sorry...

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:35.160
Really, I didn't mean to.

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:36.150
He made Fool cry, chirp.

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:37.630
What a mess, chirp.

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:39.590
He's a bad man, chirp.

00:10:39.590 --> 00:10:41.450
Chirpity-chirp! Chirp!

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:53.880
<b>Kenzaki Transport</b>

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:57.300
Good morning!

00:11:00.210 --> 00:11:01.220
...ning.

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:04.390
<i>At least they returned the greeting, huh?</i>

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:07.730
Okay, about today's job...

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:10.430
Careful, it's heavy.

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:12.810
No, it isn't...

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:14.450
This is heavy, too.

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:15.670
I bet it isn't—

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:18.930
It really is?

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:24.090
<i>I put both on jobs that could be done alone.</i>

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:26.330
<i>But how are they doing?</i>

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:29.940
Um, I'm done.

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:31.670
Already?

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:32.540
Yes.

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:33.920
Then...

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:37.840
Could you clean up the stuff 
on the floor there?

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:38.820
Sure.

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:41.780
I'm also done.

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:43.100
You, too?

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:46.360
Then, please clean up with Kawashima-san.

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:47.260
Okay.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:52.400
<i>They're more efficient than yesterday.</i>

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:55.060
<i>They both find working alone easier.</i>

00:11:58.060 --> 00:11:59.900
I'm starving!

00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:02.820
Today, it's a Hamburg steak lunch, huh?

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:05.240
Here you go, Sasaki-san... Kawashima-san.

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:07.660
Thanks.

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:09.310
Thank you.

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:14.280
Um, I'm going to get something to drink.

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:15.580
Want anything?

00:12:16.770 --> 00:12:19.250
Some tea, then.

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:20.550
Got it.

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:29.040
I go to deliver this package, and the girl 
comes out in nothing but a towel.

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:30.670
So that really happens!

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:32.230
It happened to me once, too.

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:33.090
Seriously?

00:12:33.090 --> 00:12:35.100
In my case, it was a naked, old man.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:36.810
What the heck?

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:42.860
<i>So it isn't that they don't 
like talking to people.</i>

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:47.930
<i>They will if they can't 
see the person's face?</i>

00:12:47.930 --> 00:12:49.920
<i>How does that work?</i>

00:12:51.710 --> 00:12:56.160
<i>I've also been misunderstood after 
saying what I was thinking.</i>

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:58.940
<i>Sometimes, even when looking at someone,</i>

00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:01.380
<i>I couldn't say what I wanted.</i>

00:13:01.930 --> 00:13:03.670
<i>I couldn't tell them anything...</i>

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:09.130
<i>Even if you say something directly, 
having people understand you can be difficult.</i>

00:13:09.780 --> 00:13:10.750
<i>But...</i>

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:15.400
<i>I know something that's even more enjoyable.</i>

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:21.710
<i>No one will teach you that.</i>

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:23.670
<i>You have to feel it for yourself,</i>

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:26.570
<i>and build it up, little by little.</i>

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:29.790
<i>That's what makes you who you are.</i>

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:35.770
<i>It isn't that they don't want 
to talk to me, right?</i>

00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:39.630
Are you guys done?

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:41.030
I'll put your trays away.

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:42.550
Yeah.

00:13:42.830 --> 00:13:43.870
Thanks.

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:49.930
<i>Now, it's just a matter of timing!</i>

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:57.500
We're almost done! Let's keep at it!

00:13:57.500 --> 00:13:58.350
Yeah.

00:13:58.350 --> 00:13:59.210
Okay.

00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:03.710
I'm sorry!

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:05.500
We need three hundred packages done, ASAP.

00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:06.690
Three hundred?

00:14:06.690 --> 00:14:09.320
A really good customer asked. 
I'm counting on you.

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:10.980
Oh, well. Let's do it.

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:12.570
Let's get fired up, guys.

00:14:12.570 --> 00:14:13.220
Right!

00:14:13.220 --> 00:14:14.200
Okay.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:18.080
We'll do the ones going to Kanto.

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:19.720
Inaba, you do Kansai.

00:14:19.720 --> 00:14:22.180
Sasaki and Kawashima, you take Shikoku.

00:14:22.180 --> 00:14:22.930
Right.

00:14:22.930 --> 00:14:23.800
Okay.

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:26.350
When you're done, help the others.

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:27.040
Got it?

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:28.220
Yes, sir!

00:14:43.540 --> 00:14:44.950
It's over...

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:46.340
I'm so tired.

00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:48.240
I can't move.

00:14:49.340 --> 00:14:50.160
But...

00:14:51.730 --> 00:14:54.700
That was kind of fun, maybe.

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:57.200
Yeah, I know what you mean.

00:14:58.400 --> 00:14:59.480
Me, too.

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:01.130
It was fun.

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:06.960
<b> Kenzaki Transport</b>

00:15:07.430 --> 00:15:08.880
Good morning!

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:11.300
Good morning.

00:15:11.630 --> 00:15:12.590
Morning.

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:14.140
Good morning.

00:15:15.070 --> 00:15:16.720
Everyone's here, right?

00:15:17.110 --> 00:15:19.610
What's up, boss?

00:15:19.610 --> 00:15:20.720
Well...

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:25.400
There was a problem 
with that rush job we did.

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:27.570
Were they not in time?

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:33.320
<b>Keep Upright</b>

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:33.320
A packaged marked "Keep Upright" 
was delivered upside-down.

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:41.290
It was for Shikoku.

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:42.290
Shikoku...

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:44.070
Sasaki. Kawashima.

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:45.770
That was your job, right?

00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:46.460
Well?

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:48.800
Uh...

00:15:49.350 --> 00:15:50.370
Um...

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:52.880
Well?! Did you pack it upside-down?

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:54.970
U-Um...

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:58.850
<b>Keep Upright</b>

00:15:55.380 --> 00:15:58.850
What does "Keep Upright" mean?

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:06.940
Um...

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:08.470
I see...

00:16:08.470 --> 00:16:10.440
You didn't know, huh?

00:16:12.850 --> 00:16:13.530
Kawa—

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:15.200
I'm sorry!

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:18.500
Yama-san...

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:23.220
It's my responsibility for not teaching 
them what "Keep Upright" meant!

00:16:23.220 --> 00:16:28.510
I'm terribly sorry for causing problems 
for the customer and the company!

00:16:29.620 --> 00:16:32.970
I was in charge of teaching them, 
and I didn't realize, either.

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:34.300
I'm sorry!

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:44.290
Only one package was placed upside-down, 
and the damage was minimal.

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:46.280
That's the one good thing.

00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:49.320
Make sure it doesn't happen again.

00:16:49.620 --> 00:16:50.920
Please.

00:16:58.380 --> 00:17:00.020
U-Um...

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:01.580
We...

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:07.390
"Keep Upright" means that you 
can't pack it upside-down.

00:17:07.390 --> 00:17:10.000
It had this red sticker on it, right?

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:13.920
If you don't know what something means, ask.

00:17:14.290 --> 00:17:16.450
You can ask Inaba or me.

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:17.590
Yeah.

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:20.010
Okay...

00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:25.850
<b>Kenzaki Transport</b>

00:17:30.740 --> 00:17:31.690
Um...

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:35.500
They said there was damage.

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:39.730
Oh, it's better not to think 
about it too much.

00:17:39.730 --> 00:17:41.450
Everyone messes things up.

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:46.370
But is the damage something 
we have to pay for?

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:47.790
<i>That's what's bothering him?!</i>

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:50.260
I wondered that, as well.

00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:51.500
<i>You, too?!</i>

00:17:53.080 --> 00:17:56.480
You know our boss wouldn't 
do anything so petty.

00:17:56.890 --> 00:17:58.930
Don't worry.

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:00.180
I see...

00:18:01.750 --> 00:18:06.720
<i>From the look of it, they don't know 
why Yama-san was bowing like that.</i>

00:18:08.800 --> 00:18:11.600
When I was in elementary school...

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:18.890
You know how someone always 
messes around during cleaning?

00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:23.210
Even when the team leader told 
him to cut it out, he didn't.

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:26.040
And he ended up breaking a window.

00:18:26.310 --> 00:18:28.730
The teacher came and got mad, right?

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:31.130
And the team leader said...

00:18:31.530 --> 00:18:34.970
It's my fault. I couldn't stop him.

00:18:34.970 --> 00:18:38.930
Um... Well, clean it up.

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:44.430
Because he'd apologized first, 
the teacher couldn't be angry.

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:48.310
Of course, it was partly the 
team leader's responsibility.

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:51.650
But he tried to keep the boy who broke 
it from getting in trouble, see?

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:56.070
We should thank Yama-san.

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:56.780
Yeah.

00:18:57.290 --> 00:18:59.740
And apologize to the boss.

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:02.880
The sooner, the better.

00:19:07.360 --> 00:19:08.230
Yama-san...

00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:09.050
Yama-san.

00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:16.050
<i>Worries, dumb mistakes,</i>

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:17.880
<i>nervousness, frustrations...</i>

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:22.200
<i>I hope, someday, they can all 
become good memories.</i>

00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:29.510
I worked hard over my three-day break!

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:32.350
Master...

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:37.440
I was moved by what you said back there.

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:39.530
Oh, about the cleaning?

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:43.140
An average man could not have 
brought himself to apologize

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:44.610
if it were another's fault.

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:48.450
Such self-sacrifice! Such devotion to others!

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:53.210
There's more to that story.

00:19:54.150 --> 00:19:59.300
The one who covered for the boy 
who broke the window was Hase.

00:20:00.460 --> 00:20:02.410
Wow, Hase.

00:20:02.410 --> 00:20:04.840
I couldn't have done that.

00:20:04.840 --> 00:20:06.330
What are you talking about?

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:08.970
Now, that idiot owes me.

00:20:10.470 --> 00:20:14.480
I was getting pissed off because 
he never does any cleaning...

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:17.690
Now, I can shut him up for a good long while.

00:20:19.140 --> 00:20:20.100
Yeah.

00:20:24.180 --> 00:20:27.490
Let's not tell Sasaki-sama 
and Kawashima-sama.

00:20:28.130 --> 00:20:30.070
Of course not.

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:33.640
He's always been pretty clever...

00:20:41.580 --> 00:20:44.160
I can feel it spreading through my body!

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:47.100
Real French cognac has a 
totally different aroma.

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:48.560
It's so good!

00:20:48.560 --> 00:20:50.730
Are these curry-flavored sausages?

00:20:51.160 --> 00:20:54.490
It's German soul food, currywurst.

00:20:54.490 --> 00:20:57.060
They go so well with beer!

00:20:57.060 --> 00:20:59.870
I heard that this is called a scone!

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:05.950
Hey, Inaba.

00:21:07.030 --> 00:21:09.700
You're back from Europe?

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:11.090
Just today.

00:21:11.090 --> 00:21:12.870
Here's your present.

00:21:16.630 --> 00:21:19.170
Hase-kun, come and join us!

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:21.000
Let's eat together!

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:23.760
Tell us about your trip.

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:25.510
Sure thing.

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:30.510
Just as you said, Hase-sama is very clever.

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:35.250
And the view from the castle is 
so good, it'll change your life!

00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:36.080
Yeah.

00:23:10.820 --> 00:23:13.500
Hello! My name is Fool!

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:14.860
How do you do?

00:23:14.860 --> 00:23:16.150
What are you doing, Fool?

00:23:16.150 --> 00:23:19.710
It's almost time for the social 
with the Foreigners Club!

00:23:19.710 --> 00:23:22.060
I'm practicing my introductions, 
so I won't be rude.

00:23:22.060 --> 00:23:24.200
Nice to meet you.

00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:27.230
You aren't going to be showing 
yourself to them, right?

00:23:27.230 --> 00:23:27.880
Ah.

00:23:28.300 --> 00:23:31.260
Next time on <i>Elegant Yokai Apartment Life</i>:

00:23:31.260 --> 00:23:32.740
Let's Communication.

00:23:31.260 --> 00:23:33.140
<b>Nineteenth Haunting 
Let's Communication</b>

00:23:33.130 --> 00:23:36.220
I understand exactly what's bothering her.
